      "Does Canada accept a 1968 Vienna international driving permit?",
      "It rests on no treaty. Canada is a contracting party to the 1949 Geneva Convention on Road Traffic and never joined the 1968 Vienna Convention, so if your licensing authority issues both formats, ask for the Geneva booklet. Most European authorities still can. Rental counters do look at which convention is printed on the cover."
